  "nl_text": "The database schema named \"schemabench_0122\" contains 11 tables.\nThe \"authors\" table is used to store information about authors. It has columns for author ID (au_id), last name (au_lname), first name (au_fname), phone number (phone), address (address), city (city), state (state), zip code (zip), and a contract flag (contract).\nThe \"discounts\" table is used to store information about discounts. It has columns for discount type (discounttype), store ID (stor_id), low quantity (lowqty), high quantity (highqty), and discount (discount). The store ID is a foreign key referencing the \"stores\" table.\nThe \"employee\" table is used to store information about employees. It has columns for employee ID (emp_id), first name (fname), middle initial (minit), last name (lname), job ID (job_id), job level (job_lvl), publisher ID (pub_id), and hire date (hire_date). The job ID and publisher ID are foreign keys referencing the \"jobs\" and \"publishers\" tables respectively.\nThe \"jobs\" table is used to store information about jobs. It has columns for job ID (job_id), job description (job_desc), minimum level (min_lvl), and maximum level (max_lvl).\nThe \"pub_info\" table is used to store information about publishers. It has columns for publisher ID (pub_id), logo (logo), and publisher information (pr_info). The publisher ID is a foreign key referencing the \"publishers\" table.\nThe \"publishers\" table is used to store information about publishers. It has columns for publisher ID (pub_id), publisher name (pub_name), city (city), state (state), and country (country).\nThe \"roysched\" table is used to store information about royalties. It has columns for title ID (title_id), low range (lorange), high range (hirange), and royalty (royalty). The title ID is a foreign key referencing the \"titles\" table.\nThe \"sales\" table is used to store information about sales. It has columns for store ID (stor_id), order number (ord_num), order date (ord_date), quantity (qty), payment terms (payterms), and title ID (title_id). The store ID and title ID are foreign keys referencing the \"stores\" and \"titles\" tables respectively.\nThe \"stores\" table is used to store information about stores. It has columns for store ID (stor_id), store name (stor_name), store address (stor_address), city (city), state (state), and zip code (zip).\nThe \"titleauthor\" table is used to store information about authors and their contributions to titles. It has columns for author ID (au_id), title ID (title_id), author order (au_ord), and royalty percentage (royaltyper). The title ID and author ID are foreign keys referencing the \"titles\" and \"authors\" tables respectively.\nThe \"titles\" table is used to store information about titles. It has columns for title ID (title_id), title (title), type (type), publisher ID (pub_id), price (price), advance (advance), royalty (royalty), year-to-date sales (ytd_sales), notes (notes), and publication date (pubdate). The publisher ID is a foreign key referencing the \"publishers\" table.",
  "gold_question": "1) Background / Context\n\nThis project involves developing a system for a book publishing company. The company's database is designed to manage various aspects related to authors, books, sales, and employees. The system will support the operational and decision-making processes within the publishing environment.\n\n2) Objectives\n\nThe primary objective is to design a database management system that facilitates efficient tracking and management of authors, book sales, employee information, and publisher details. The system should provide accurate data to support sales analysis, royalty management, and operational reporting.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Stakeholders:\n  - Publishing Company Management\n  - Sales and Marketing Teams\n  - HR Department\n\n- Users:\n  - Administrators\n  - Sales Personnel\n  - Authors\n  - Employees\n\n4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- Author Management: Store and manage comprehensive details about authors, including names, contact information, contractual status, and associated titles.\n\n- Book Management: Maintain detailed information on book titles, types, prices, publication dates, and related royalties. Handle data related to publishers and publication details.\n\n- Sales Tracking: Record and manage sales data, including order numbers, quantities sold, stores involved, and payment terms. Support the analysis of sales trends and performance.\n\n- Royalty Scheduling: Implement a system to schedule and compute royalties, offering range-based royalty management connected to sales quantities.\n\n- Employee Management: Track employee data, including personal details, job roles, and employment history within the publishing company.\n\n- Discount Management: Organize and apply discount structures based on quantity, offering flexibility to different stores.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Scalability: The system should effectively handle a growing number of authors, titles, and sales transactions without performance degradation.\n\n- Security: Implement robust security measures to protect sensitive author and financial data, ensuring compliance with relevant data protection regulations.\n\n- Usability: The system should be user-friendly, with an intuitive interface to facilitate ease of use for non-technical users.\n\n- Data Integrity: Ensure data accuracy and reliability through the enforcement of constraints, such as foreign keys and validation rules.\n\n- Maintainability: The system architecture should support easy updates and modifications to accommodate future business needs or technology advancements.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_deepseek/0122.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0122\nCREATE TABLE `authors` (\n  `au_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `au_lname` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `au_fname` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `city` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `state` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `zip` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `contract` tinyint(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`au_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `discounts` (\n  `discounttype` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `stor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `lowqty` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `highqty` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `discount` decimal(5,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`discounttype`, `stor_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `discounts_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`stor_id`) REFERENCES `stores` (`stor_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employee` (\n  `emp_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `fname` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `minit` char(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `lname` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `job_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `job_lvl` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `pub_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `hire_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`emp_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`job_id`) REFERENCES `jobs` (`job_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`pub_id`) REFERENCES `publishers` (`pub_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `jobs` (\n  `job_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `job_desc` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `min_lvl` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `max_lvl` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`job_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `pub_info` (\n  `pub_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `logo` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `pr_info` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`pub_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `pub_info_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`pub_id`) REFERENCES `publishers` (`pub_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `publishers` (\n  `pub_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `pub_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `city` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `state` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `country` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`pub_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `roysched` (\n  `title_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `lorange` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `hirange` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `royalty` decimal(5,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`title_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `roysched_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`title_id`) REFERENCES `titles` (`title_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sales` (\n  `stor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `ord_num` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `ord_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `qty` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `payterms` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `title_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`stor_id`, `ord_num`),\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`stor_id`) REFERENCES `stores` (`stor_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`title_id`) REFERENCES `titles` (`title_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `stores` (\n  `stor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `stor_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `stor_address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `city` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `state` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `zip` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`stor_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `titleauthor` (\n  `au_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `au_ord` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `royaltyper` decimal(5,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`au_id`, `title_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `titleauthor_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`au_id`) REFERENCES `authors` (`au_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `titleauthor_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`title_id`) REFERENCES `titles` (`title_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `titles` (\n  `title_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `pub_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `advance` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `royalty` decimal(5,2) NOT NULL,\n  `ytd_sales` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `notes` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `pubdate` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`title_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `titles_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`pub_id`) REFERENCES `publishers` (`pub_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
